  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Multi-Head Attention** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np, math\n\ndef dl_multi_head_attention(x: list, num_heads: int = 2) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(x, dtype=float)\n    N, D = arr.shape\n    dk = D // num_heads\n    q = arr.reshape(N, num_heads, dk).transpose(1, 0, 2)\n    s = (q @ q.transpose(0, 2, 1)) / math.sqrt(dk)\n    e = np.exp(s - np.max(s, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    attn = e / np.sum(e, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    return np.round((attn @ q).transpose(1, 0, 2).reshape(N, D), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
